2026-11-05T14:24:03.191+08:00 DEBUG 57044 --- [agentscope-agent-server] [loomBoundedElastic-4] i.a.e.model.ollama.OllamaHttpClient      : Ollama streaming request to http://192.168.0.235:11435/api/chat: {"model":"qwen3:14b","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"你是一个具备工具调用能力的智能助手。\n可用能力:自定义 Java 工具、MCP 工具(前缀 mcp__)、以及技能(Skill)目录。\n共享工作区目录: D:\\demo\\agent_01\\workspace\n使用文件系统类工具时,优先把文件读写限制在该工作区内。\n当某个技能与当前任务相关时,先加载/阅读该技能再按其指引执行。\n用户可能上传了参考文档:问题涉及文档内容时,先调用 list_context_files 查看,\n再用 read_document 读取正文后作答;与文档无关的问题不必调用这两个工具。\n回答使用简体中文,除非用户另有要求。\n## Available Skills\n\n<usage>\nSkills provide specialized capabilities and domain knowledge. Use them when they match your current task.\n\nHow to use skills:\n- Load skill: load_skill_through_path(skillId=\"<skill-id>\", path=\"SKILL.md\")\n- The skill will be activated and its documentation loaded with detailed instructions\n- Additional resources (scripts, assets, references) can be loaded using the same tool with different paths\n\nExample:\n1. User asks to analyze data → find a matching skill below (e.g. <skill-id>data-analysis_builtin</skill-id>)\n2. Load it: load_skill_through_path(skillId=\"data-analysis_builtin\", path=\"SKILL.md\")\n3. Follow the instructions returned by the skill\n\nMetadata is rendered as XML under each <skill> element:\n- scalar metadata becomes a simple child element\n- nested maps become nested XML elements\n- lists become repeated <item> elements\n- <skill-id> is always appended for tool loading\n</usage>\n\n<available_skills>\n\n<skill>\n  <name>livelihood-query</name>\n  <description>民生查询功能。当用户询问天气(气温/下雨/要不要带伞/未来几天天气)或快递物流(单号轨迹/包裹到哪了/发货签收状态)时使用,调用 query_weather 与 query_express 两个工具给出准确数据。</description>\n  <skill-id>livelihood-query_filesystem-agent_01_skills</skill-id>\n</skill>\n\n<skill>\n  <name>weekly-report</name>\n  <description>当用户需要生成周报/工作汇报时使用。优先读取用户上传到&quot;参考文档&quot;文件夹的原始材料(日志/文档/表格),其次查看工作区内的笔记文件,汇总产出结构化中文周报。</description>\n  <skill-id>weekly-report_filesystem-agent_01_skills</skill-id>\n</skill>\n\n</available_skills>"},{"role":"user","content":"【参考文档目录】本 agent 现有 1 个用户上传的参考文档:\n- CDC.md (12.5 KB)\n当用户的问题涉及上述文档内容时,先调用 read_document 工具(参数填上表中的精确文件名)获取正文后再作答,不要凭猜测回答、也不要把工具调用当成文本输出;与文档无关的问题请忽略本目录。\n标记: ctx-fingerprint:5ee02bc6aa741857\n\n【用户本轮提问】\n北京今天天气怎么样？"},{"role":"assistant","thinking":"好的，用户问的是北京今天的天气怎么样。首先，我需要确定是否需要使用参考文档。根据用户提供的参考文档目录，有一个CDC.md文件，但用户的问题是关于天气的，而CDC通常指疾病控制中心，可能和天气无关。因此，可能不需要调用read_document工具来读取参考文档。\n\n接下来，查看可用的技能。有一个livelihood-query技能，描述中提到当用户询问天气时使用，调用query_weather工具。所以应该使用这个技能来处理天气查询。\n\n然后，检查工具列表中的query_weather函数。该函数需要城市名和预报天数，城市名可以是中文或拼音，预报天数默认是3天，但用户只问今天，所以可能需要设置为0。不过用户的问题只是今天的情况，可能不需要未来几天的预报，但根据函数描述，不填默认是3天。不过用户的问题只关注今天，所以可能需要设置forecast_days为0。\n\n不过，用户的问题只是“今天”，所以可能只需要当前实况，即forecast_days设为0。但需要确认函数参数，forecast_days的描述是“附带未来几天的预报，整数0-3；填0表示只要当前实况，不填默认3”。所以正确的参数应该是city为“北京”，forecast_days为0。\n\n不过，用户的问题可能只需要当前天气，不需要未来预报，所以调用query_weather时，参数应为北京和0。但可能用户没有明确说不需要未来几天，所以可能默认返回当前和未来三天。不过根据问题，用户只关心今天，所以可能更准确的是设置为0。\n\n不过，可能用户的问题中的“今天”只是询问当前天气，而函数默认返回当前和未来三天，但用户可能只需要当前的情况。不过根据函数说明，填0的话只返回当前实况。所以正确的参数是city: \"北京\"，forecast_days: 0。\n\n但可能用户没有明确说明是否需要未来几天，所以可能需要调用默认参数，即不填forecast_days，返回当前和未来三天。但用户的问题只是问今天，可能只需要当前天气。需要根据函数参数来决定。\n\n不过，根据用户的问题，直接回答当前天气即可，所以设置forecast_days为0。因此，调用query_weather函数，参数是city: \"北京\"，forecast_days: 0。\n\n不过，可能用户的问题中的“今天”只是询问当前天气，而函数默认返回当前和未来三天，但用户可能只需要当前的情况。所以正确的参数是forecast_days设为0。\n\n综上，应该调用query_weather工具，参数为北京和0，得到当前天气情况。\n","tool_calls":[{"function":{"name":"query_weather","arguments":{"city":"北京","forecast_days":0}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"\"天气查询失败: Illegal character ((CTRL-CHAR, code 31)): only regular white space (\\\\r, \\\\n, \\\\t) is allowed between tokens\\n at [Source: REDACTED (`StreamReadFeature.INCLUDE_SOURCE_IN_LOCATION` disabled); line: 1, column: 2]\"","tool_call_id":"f4657733-6791-4ed7-8ebc-f86b67cf7ebe","tool_name":"query_weather"},{"role":"assistant","thinking":"好的，用户再次询问北京的天气，但之前的query_weather调用失败了，错误信息是“Illegal character ((CTRL-CHAR, code 31)): only regular white space (\\r, \\n, \\t) is allowed between tokens”。这可能意味着在请求参数中存在非法字符，或者API的调用方式有问题。\n\n首先，我需要检查用户的问题是否正确。用户的问题是“北京今天天气怎么样？”，看起来没问题。之前的调用参数是{\"city\":\"北京\",\"forecast_days\":0}，可能参数格式有问题，或者API需要不同的参数结构。\n\n查看query_weather的工具描述，参数是[city forecast_days]，其中forecast_days是整数，范围0-3。可能参数应该用空格分隔，而不是JSON格式？或者可能工具的参数需要调整。\n\n或者，可能在调用工具时，参数传递的方式有误。例如，可能应该将参数作为字符串传递，而不是JSON对象。例如，正确的调用可能是{\"name\": \"query_weather\", \"arguments\": \"北京 0\"}，而不是JSON对象。\n\n但根据之前的工具定义，query_weather的参数是[city forecast_days]，所以可能参数应该是一个字符串，用空格分隔。可能之前的调用使用了JSON格式，而工具期望的是字符串参数。\n\n因此，需要调整调用方式，将参数作为字符串传递，例如\"北京 0\"，而不是JSON对象。这样可能解决非法字符的问题，因为可能JSON格式中的引号或其他字符被错误处理。\n\n所以，正确的调用应该是：\n\n{\"name\": \"query_weather\", \"arguments\": \"北京 0\"}\n\n这样参数以字符串形式传递，避免了可能的非法字符问题。需要再次尝试调用，使用正确的参数格式。\n"},{"role":"user","content":"<system-reminder>Your previous reply had empty content - the full answer was written to the reasoning channel only. Reply again and write the final answer into the content channel.</system-reminder>"}],"stream":true,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"move_file","description":"Move or rename files and directories. Can move files between directories and rename them in a single operation. If the destination exists, the operation will fail. Works across different directories and can be used for simple renaming within the same directory. Both source and destination must be within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"destination":{"type":"string"},"source":{"type":"string"}},"required":["source","destination"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"directory_tree","description":"Get a recursive tree view of files and directories as a JSON structure. Each entry includes 'name', 'type' (file/directory), and 'children' for directories. Files have no children array, while directories always have a children array (which may be empty). The output is formatted with 2-space indentation for readability. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"excludePatterns":{"default":[],"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_context_files","description":"Lists all reference / context documents uploaded by the user for this agent. Call this BEFORE reading any document so you know what references are available. Returns each file's name, size, and last modified time.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_allowed_directories","description":"Returns the list of directories that this server is allowed to access. Subdirectories within these allowed directories are also accessible. Use this to understand which directories and their nested paths are available before trying to access files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_directory","description":"Get a detailed listing of all files and directories in a specified path. Results clearly distinguish between files and directories with [FILE] and [DIR] prefixes. This tool is essential for understanding directory structure and finding specific files within a directory. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_text_file","description":"Read the complete contents of a file from the file system as text. Handles various text encodings and provides detailed error messages if the file cannot be read. Use this tool when you need to examine the contents of a single file. Use the 'head' parameter to read only the first N lines of a file, or the 'tail' parameter to read only the last N lines of a file. Operates on the file as text regardless of extension. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"head":{"description":"If provided, returns only the first N lines of the file","type":"number"},"path":{"type":"string"},"tail":{"description":"If provided, returns only the last N lines of the file","type":"number"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_file","description":"Read the complete contents of a file as text. DEPRECATED: Use read_text_file instead.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"head":{"description":"If provided, returns only the first N lines of the file","type":"number"},"path":{"type":"string"},"tail":{"description":"If provided, returns only the last N lines of the file","type":"number"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"query_express","description":"Tracks an express delivery by its waybill number via ShowAPI 64-19 (万维易源). Use it when the user asks where their package/快递/物流 is. Carrier is auto-detected by default(com=auto); if auto fails, pass com with the pinyin abbreviation like shunfeng/youzhengguonei. 顺丰/跨越/中通/壹米滴答/信丰 must pass phone=收件人手机号后四位。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"carrier":{"type":"string","description":"快递公司字母简称,可不填(默认 auto 自动识别)。 auto 识别失败时指定,如: shunfeng顺丰 youzhengguonei邮政 yuantong圆通 zhongtong中通 shentong申通 yunda韵达 jd京东 jitujiuye极兔 ems"},"phone":{"type":"string","description":"收件人手机号后 4 位;顺丰/跨越/中通/壹米滴答/信丰必填,其它可不填"},"waybill_no":{"type":"string","description":"快递单号,如 SF1234567890 / 78123456789012"}},"required":["waybill_no","carrier","phone"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"load_skill_through_path","description":"Load and activate a skill resource by its ID and resource path.\n\n**Functionality:**\n1. Activates the specified skill for this session (adding its tool groups to this session's active set)\n2. Returns the requested resource content\n\n**Path rules:**\n- Use path=\"SKILL.md\" to load the skill's markdown documentation (name, description, usage instructions).\n- Use exact resource paths listed by the skill, such as \"references/guide.md\" or \"scripts/run.py\".\n- Do not use '.', './', the skill directory, or an absolute path.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["skillId","path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"The exact resource path within the skill. Use 'SKILL.md' to load the skill instructions. Do not use '.', './', directories, or absolute paths."},"skillId":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the skill."}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_document","description":"Parses a reference/context document (PDF, Word, PPT, Excel, Markdown, CSV, plain text, HTML, etc.) and returns its textual content. File must be in the agent's context folder (use list_context_files first). Returns up to 12000 characters per document; longer files are truncated.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"filename":{"type":"string","description":"Exact filename of the document inside the context folder, e.g. 'weekly-report-2026-11-03.docx' (no path, just the file name)"}},"required":["filename"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"query_weather","description":"Queries real-time weather and the coming days forecast for a Chinese city via QWeather free API. Use it whenever the user asks about weather, temperature, rain/snow, or whether to bring an umbrella. Returns current conditions plus daily forecast.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"city":{"type":"string","description":"城市名,如: 北京 / 上海 / 深圳(中文或拼音)"},"forecast_days":{"type":"integer","description":"附带未来几天的预报,整数 0-3;填 0 表示只要当前实况,不填默认 3"}},"required":["city","forecast_days"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"create_directory","description":"Create a new directory or ensure a directory exists. Can create multiple nested directories in one operation. If the directory already exists, this operation will succeed silently. Perfect for setting up directory structures for projects or ensuring required paths exist. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_multiple_files","description":"Read the contents of multiple files simultaneously. This is more efficient than reading files one by one when you need to analyze or compare multiple files. Each file's content is returned with its path as a reference. Failed reads for individual files won't stop the entire operation. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"paths":{"minItems":1,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Array of file paths to read. Each path must be a string pointing to a valid file within allowed directories."}},"required":["paths"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"calc_text_stats","description":"Counts characters, lines and words of the given text.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string","description":"The text to analyze"}},"required":["text"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_directory_with_sizes","description":"Get a detailed listing of all files and directories in a specified path, including sizes. Results clearly distinguish between files and directories with [FILE] and [DIR] prefixes. This tool is useful for understanding directory structure and finding specific files within a directory. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"sortBy":{"default":"name","description":"Sort entries by name or size","type":"string","enum":["name","size"]}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"get_workspace_info","description":"Returns the absolute path of the shared workspace directory. MCP file tools are rooted here, so other file paths used by the agent should be relative to this directory.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","description":"Make line-based edits to a text file. Each edit replaces exact line sequences with new content. Returns a git-style diff showing the changes made. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Text to search for - must match exactly"},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Text to replace with"}},"required":["oldText","newText"]}},"dryRun":{"default":false,"description":"Preview changes using git-style diff format","type":"boolean"}},"required":["path","edits"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","description":"Create a new file or completely overwrite an existing file with new content. Use with caution as it will overwrite existing files without warning. Handles text content with proper encoding. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"content":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path","content"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"get_file_info","description":"Retrieve detailed metadata about a file or directory. Returns comprehensive information including size, creation time, last modified time, permissions, and type. This tool is perfect for understanding file characteristics without reading the actual content. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"get_current_time","description":"Returns the current date and time in a given IANA timezone.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"timezone":{"type":"string","description":"IANA timezone, e.g. Asia/Shanghai"}},"required":["timezone"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_media_file","description":"Read a file and return it as a base64-encoded content block with its MIME type. Image and audio files are returned as image/audio content; any other file type is returned as an embedded resource. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"search_files","description":"Recursively search for files and directories matching a pattern. The patterns should be glob-style patterns that match paths relative to the working directory. Use pattern like '*.ext' to match files in current directory, and '**/*.ext' to match files in all subdirectories. Returns full paths to all matching items. Great for finding files when you don't know their exact location. Only searches within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"pattern":{"type":"string"},"excludePatterns":{"default":[],"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path","pattern"]}}}],"options":{"temperature":0.7}}
