2026-11-05T14:28:38.266+08:00 DEBUG 34636 --- [agentscope-agent-server] [loomBoundedElastic-7] i.a.e.model.ollama.OllamaHttpClient      : Ollama streaming request to http://192.168.0.235:11435/api/chat: {"model":"qwen3:14b","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"你是一个具备工具调用能力的智能助手。\n可用能力:自定义 Java 工具、MCP 工具(前缀 mcp__)、以及技能(Skill)目录。\n共享工作区目录: D:\\demo\\agent_01\\workspace\n使用文件系统类工具时,优先把文件读写限制在该工作区内。\n当某个技能与当前任务相关时,先加载/阅读该技能再按其指引执行。\n用户可能上传了参考文档:问题涉及文档内容时,先调用 list_context_files 查看,\n再用 read_document 读取正文后作答;与文档无关的问题不必调用这两个工具。\n回答使用简体中文,除非用户另有要求。\n## Available Skills\n\n<usage>\nSkills provide specialized capabilities and domain knowledge. Use them when they match your current task.\n\nHow to use skills:\n- Load skill: load_skill_through_path(skillId=\"<skill-id>\", path=\"SKILL.md\")\n- The skill will be activated and its documentation loaded with detailed instructions\n- Additional resources (scripts, assets, references) can be loaded using the same tool with different paths\n\nExample:\n1. User asks to analyze data → find a matching skill below (e.g. <skill-id>data-analysis_builtin</skill-id>)\n2. Load it: load_skill_through_path(skillId=\"data-analysis_builtin\", path=\"SKILL.md\")\n3. Follow the instructions returned by the skill\n\nMetadata is rendered as XML under each <skill> element:\n- scalar metadata becomes a simple child element\n- nested maps become nested XML elements\n- lists become repeated <item> elements\n- <skill-id> is always appended for tool loading\n</usage>\n\n<available_skills>\n\n<skill>\n  <name>livelihood-query</name>\n  <description>民生查询功能。当用户询问天气(气温/下雨/要不要带伞/未来几天天气)或快递物流(单号轨迹/包裹到哪了/发货签收状态)时使用,调用 query_weather 与 query_express 两个工具给出准确数据。</description>\n  <skill-id>livelihood-query_filesystem-agent_01_skills</skill-id>\n</skill>\n\n<skill>\n  <name>weekly-report</name>\n  <description>当用户需要生成周报/工作汇报时使用。优先读取用户上传到&quot;参考文档&quot;文件夹的原始材料(日志/文档/表格),其次查看工作区内的笔记文件,汇总产出结构化中文周报。</description>\n  <skill-id>weekly-report_filesystem-agent_01_skills</skill-id>\n</skill>\n\n</available_skills>"},{"role":"user","content":"【参考文档目录】本 agent 现有 1 个用户上传的参考文档:\n- CDC.md (12.5 KB)\n当用户的问题涉及上述文档内容时,先调用 read_document 工具(参数填上表中的精确文件名)获取正文后再作答,不要凭猜测回答、也不要把工具调用当成文本输出;与文档无关的问题请忽略本目录。\n标记: ctx-fingerprint:5ee02bc6aa741857\n\n【用户本轮提问】\n帮我查下快递单号 78123456789012 到哪了？"},{"role":"assistant","thinking":"好的，用户让我帮忙查询快递单号78123456789012的状态。首先，我需要确定使用哪个工具。根据可用的工具列表，有一个query_express函数，专门用于跟踪快递物流信息。\n\n接下来，检查单号的格式是否正确。用户提供的单号是78123456789012，看起来是14位数字，这可能属于某些快递公司，比如中通、圆通等。不过，根据query_express的参数说明，某些快递公司如顺丰、中通等需要提供收件人手机号的后四位。但用户没有提供手机号，所以可能需要先确认快递公司，或者自动识别。\n\n根据query_express的参数，carrier参数可以自动识别，如果自动识别失败，可能需要手动指定。但用户的问题中没有提到快递公司，所以可能需要先用自动识别。不过，单号的前缀可能有助于判断快递公司。例如，中通的单号通常以78开头，所以可能需要指定carrier为zhongtong，并且需要手机号后四位。但用户没有提供手机号，这可能会导致查询失败。\n\n这时候，可能需要向用户询问手机号的后四位，但根据问题描述，用户可能希望直接处理。不过，根据工具的参数说明，如果快递公司是顺丰、中通等，必须提供手机号后四位。因此，可能需要先检查是否需要手机号，如果需要的话，可能需要提示用户。但用户的问题中没有给出，所以可能需要假设自动识别可以成功，或者尝试查询。\n\n不过，根据工具的参数，如果自动识别失败，可能需要手动指定carrier。所以，可能需要先调用query_express，使用默认的carrier=auto，看看是否能成功。如果失败，可能需要进一步处理，但当前情况下，先尝试自动识别。\n\n因此，调用query_express函数，参数waybill_no为78123456789012，carrier设为auto，phone留空。如果返回错误，可能需要用户补充信息，但根据当前信息，先执行查询。\n","tool_calls":[{"function":{"name":"query_express","arguments":{"waybill_no":"78123456789012","carrier":"auto"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"\"快递查询网关处理失败: \"","tool_call_id":"f3d9c025-30ea-4ecf-aa7a-deeda8c431c4","tool_name":"query_express"}],"stream":true,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"move_file","description":"Move or rename files and directories. Can move files between directories and rename them in a single operation. If the destination exists, the operation will fail. Works across different directories and can be used for simple renaming within the same directory. Both source and destination must be within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"destination":{"type":"string"},"source":{"type":"string"}},"required":["source","destination"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"directory_tree","description":"Get a recursive tree view of files and directories as a JSON structure. Each entry includes 'name', 'type' (file/directory), and 'children' for directories. Files have no children array, while directories always have a children array (which may be empty). The output is formatted with 2-space indentation for readability. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"excludePatterns":{"default":[],"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_context_files","description":"Lists all reference / context documents uploaded by the user for this agent. Call this BEFORE reading any document so you know what references are available. Returns each file's name, size, and last modified time.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_allowed_directories","description":"Returns the list of directories that this server is allowed to access. Subdirectories within these allowed directories are also accessible. Use this to understand which directories and their nested paths are available before trying to access files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_directory","description":"Get a detailed listing of all files and directories in a specified path. Results clearly distinguish between files and directories with [FILE] and [DIR] prefixes. This tool is essential for understanding directory structure and finding specific files within a directory. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_text_file","description":"Read the complete contents of a file from the file system as text. Handles various text encodings and provides detailed error messages if the file cannot be read. Use this tool when you need to examine the contents of a single file. Use the 'head' parameter to read only the first N lines of a file, or the 'tail' parameter to read only the last N lines of a file. Operates on the file as text regardless of extension. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"head":{"description":"If provided, returns only the first N lines of the file","type":"number"},"path":{"type":"string"},"tail":{"description":"If provided, returns only the last N lines of the file","type":"number"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_file","description":"Read the complete contents of a file as text. DEPRECATED: Use read_text_file instead.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"head":{"description":"If provided, returns only the first N lines of the file","type":"number"},"path":{"type":"string"},"tail":{"description":"If provided, returns only the last N lines of the file","type":"number"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"query_express","description":"Tracks an express delivery by its waybill number via ShowAPI 64-19 (万维易源). Use it when the user asks where their package/快递/物流 is. Carrier is auto-detected by default(com=auto); if auto fails, pass com with the pinyin abbreviation like shunfeng/youzhengguonei. 顺丰/跨越/中通/壹米滴答/信丰 must pass phone=收件人手机号后四位。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"carrier":{"type":"string","description":"快递公司字母简称,可不填(默认 auto 自动识别)。 auto 识别失败时指定,如: shunfeng顺丰 youzhengguonei邮政 yuantong圆通 zhongtong中通 shentong申通 yunda韵达 jd京东 jitujiuye极兔 ems"},"phone":{"type":"string","description":"收件人手机号后 4 位;顺丰/跨越/中通/壹米滴答/信丰必填,其它可不填"},"waybill_no":{"type":"string","description":"快递单号,如 SF1234567890 / 78123456789012"}},"required":["waybill_no"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"load_skill_through_path","description":"Load and activate a skill resource by its ID and resource path.\n\n**Functionality:**\n1. Activates the specified skill for this session (adding its tool groups to this session's active set)\n2. Returns the requested resource content\n\n**Path rules:**\n- Use path=\"SKILL.md\" to load the skill's markdown documentation (name, description, usage instructions).\n- Use exact resource paths listed by the skill, such as \"references/guide.md\" or \"scripts/run.py\".\n- Do not use '.', './', the skill directory, or an absolute path.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["skillId","path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"The exact resource path within the skill. Use 'SKILL.md' to load the skill instructions. Do not use '.', './', directories, or absolute paths."},"skillId":{"type":"string","description":"The unique identifier of the skill."}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_document","description":"Parses a reference/context document (PDF, Word, PPT, Excel, Markdown, CSV, plain text, HTML, etc.) and returns its textual content. File must be in the agent's context folder (use list_context_files first). Returns up to 12000 characters per document; longer files are truncated.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"filename":{"type":"string","description":"Exact filename of the document inside the context folder, e.g. 'weekly-report-2026-11-03.docx' (no path, just the file name)"}},"required":["filename"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"query_weather","description":"Queries real-time weather and the coming days forecast for a Chinese city via QWeather free API. Use it whenever the user asks about weather, temperature, rain/snow, or whether to bring an umbrella. Returns current conditions plus daily forecast.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"city":{"type":"string","description":"城市名,如: 北京 / 上海 / 深圳(中文或拼音)"},"forecast_days":{"type":"integer","description":"附带未来几天的预报,整数 0-3;填 0 表示只要当前实况,不填默认 3"}},"required":["city"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"create_directory","description":"Create a new directory or ensure a directory exists. Can create multiple nested directories in one operation. If the directory already exists, this operation will succeed silently. Perfect for setting up directory structures for projects or ensuring required paths exist. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_multiple_files","description":"Read the contents of multiple files simultaneously. This is more efficient than reading files one by one when you need to analyze or compare multiple files. Each file's content is returned with its path as a reference. Failed reads for individual files won't stop the entire operation. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"paths":{"minItems":1,"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Array of file paths to read. Each path must be a string pointing to a valid file within allowed directories."}},"required":["paths"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"calc_text_stats","description":"Counts characters, lines and words of the given text.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string","description":"The text to analyze"}},"required":["text"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"list_directory_with_sizes","description":"Get a detailed listing of all files and directories in a specified path, including sizes. Results clearly distinguish between files and directories with [FILE] and [DIR] prefixes. This tool is useful for understanding directory structure and finding specific files within a directory. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"sortBy":{"default":"name","description":"Sort entries by name or size","type":"string","enum":["name","size"]}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"get_workspace_info","description":"Returns the absolute path of the shared workspace directory. MCP file tools are rooted here, so other file paths used by the agent should be relative to this directory.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","description":"Make line-based edits to a text file. Each edit replaces exact line sequences with new content. Returns a git-style diff showing the changes made. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Text to search for - must match exactly"},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Text to replace with"}},"required":["oldText","newText"]}},"dryRun":{"default":false,"description":"Preview changes using git-style diff format","type":"boolean"}},"required":["path","edits"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","description":"Create a new file or completely overwrite an existing file with new content. Use with caution as it will overwrite existing files without warning. Handles text content with proper encoding. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"content":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path","content"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"get_file_info","description":"Retrieve detailed metadata about a file or directory. Returns comprehensive information including size, creation time, last modified time, permissions, and type. This tool is perfect for understanding file characteristics without reading the actual content. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"get_current_time","description":"Returns the current date and time in a given IANA timezone.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"timezone":{"type":"string","description":"IANA timezone, e.g. Asia/Shanghai"}},"required":["timezone"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read_media_file","description":"Read a file and return it as a base64-encoded content block with its MIME type. Image and audio files are returned as image/audio content; any other file type is returned as an embedded resource. Only works within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"search_files","description":"Recursively search for files and directories matching a pattern. The patterns should be glob-style patterns that match paths relative to the working directory. Use pattern like '*.ext' to match files in current directory, and '**/*.ext' to match files in all subdirectories. Returns full paths to all matching items. Great for finding files when you don't know their exact location. Only searches within allowed directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"pattern":{"type":"string"},"excludePatterns":{"default":[],"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path","pattern"]}}}],"options":{"temperature":0.7}}
